{
 "note": "Ground truth for the clut corpus, written by reading each photograph at native resolution before any model was run on it. Where the photograph genuinely does not settle a quantity, qty is a two-element range and any value inside it scores correct: inventing precision the image does not carry would make the number unreadable.",
 "policy": {
  "subject": "For tier 'cart', the subject is what is inside the basket; anything on the counter around it is clutter and appears in 'ignore'. For tier 'storage', the subject is every grocery product legibly visible in the frame, including on an adjacent shelf, because there is no container to draw the line at.",
  "ignore": "Items listed in 'ignore' are neither a miss when absent nor a false positive when named. They are things a shopper is not buying: kitchen equipment, papers, a book, a mask, storage jars the household already owns, and for a refrigerator drawer the shelf above it. 'ignoreMatch' is how the scorer recognises them, and is kept narrow on purpose so that it can never absorb a misidentification of a real product.",
  "match": "A bag line counts as this product when its lowercased, accent-folded name or description contains any string in 'match'. Each line is assigned to one label: the label whose matching phrase is longest wins, a tie goes to the label with the fewest lines so far, and a line the photograph's 'ignoreMatch' also covers reaches a label only when that label has nothing yet. So two labels sharing a generic phrase ('cracker', 'milk') can both be found, and a jar of loose spaghetti beside the Barilla box does not double the box. 'brandMatch' is scored separately and only where the packaging is legible; a null brand is correct for loose produce.",
  "hidden": "true when the product is substantially occluded by another product. Requirement 3 asks that the census raise its occlusion flag on a photograph that has any of these.",
  "legible": "false when the packaging cannot be read in the photograph. Requirement 4 asks that these come back with a low confidence or a needsCloserLook, not a confident brand."
 },
